WEBVTT

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.780
Everyone's all pumped up about protecting the Green Earth,

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.640
but we do have New Years coming right around the corner,

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.690
and everyone took today off.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.830
So instead...

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.930
Oh man, it's a highlights episode!

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:18.250
Geez!

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.400
Today's Nadesico is a highlight episode?

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.700
Looks more like an introductory episode.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.340
That's because they reached the mid-point of the series.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.890
They need to organize what's happened so far.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.490
You're pretty familiar with this, Junpei.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.700
I bet it's really because

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.900
the anime company has a hard time coping with production before New Year's Eve.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.450
Geez, you're too much of a realist, Joe!

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.730
Hey! It's starting!

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:55.900
Three!

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:56.650
Two!

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.400
One!

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.770
Ka-boom!

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.370
Wow!

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.490
Hey! It's "Get to Know the Nadesico!"

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.550
Hey, everyone, come closer!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.940
It's time to talk about the secrets of the Nadesico!

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.080
Come closer.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:15.170
Today will be special with lots of stuff about the Nadesico to tell you about.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.840
Then, let me explain now.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.760
In 2195, Earth was confronting the greatest threat it had ever encountered.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.000
All hands, abandon ship!

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.260
This ship will ram the Chulip!

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.440
The mysterious army of unmanned weapons attacked Mars, and occupied it.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:37.070
The Moon fell, and they advanced toward Earth as well.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.050
The UEAF was hopelessly outgunned and unprepared.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.120
That was when the Nadesico made its debut.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.210
A high-mobile battleship designed by Nergal Heavy Industries.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.780
Designation NERGAL ND001.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:53.840
Total length, 298 meters.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:55.730
Total height, 106.8 meters.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.430
Total width, 148 meters.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.570
Total weight, 37,530 metric tons.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.740
Total crew, 214.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.810
Powered by four nuclear pulse engines and two phase transition engines.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.730
Equipped with S VC2027 "Omoikane" central mainframe computer.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:16.110
That's enough for the basic specs.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.970
Let's start our tour with the bridge, which is the topmost deck out of the 12.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.450
This is the bridge. All commands are issued from here.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.120
Captain

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.490
Oh, that's right. Today, everyone has the day off.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.870
Brake Time

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:32.220
Right below the bridge is the virtual reality room.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.980
I'll explain!

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:41.540
This room was created to relieve the crew's stress while in space.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.550
The system analyzes a person's brain waves automatically, and

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:49.590
conducts psychological analysis allowing it to fit environments for each person.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.160
Wow...

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:57.350
In here, Akito-san is my mentor in an after-school club!

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:00.400
Come on! Relax, relax!

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.910
How are we going to relieve any stress if you tense up like this?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.160
For you...

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.170
No!

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.420
Every once in a while,

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.370
there are those who come here to calm their worldly desires,

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.830
so it is sometimes referred to as the meditation room.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.610
The recreation room is on Deck 4,

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.810
outfitted with the latest model year 2195 table tennis table.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.180
And next to that is the observation deck fitted with holographic imagery,

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.530
allowing the user to customize the scenery, air pressure,

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.870
and oxygen levels according to their needs.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:49.740
Just below, Houmei-san is doing her magic in the galley.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.010
Wow, that looks wonderful!

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.790
All right, here we go!

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.790
While it's the business of our customers to be cheerful

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.840
about the year coming to a close and New Years coming up,

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:03.140
we have to keep it together, or else we can't do our jobs.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:08.060
I don't think I'm so bad myself, but it's amazing what a professional can do.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.390
The Earth is small, yet still very vast!

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.990
Each region has its own flavors!

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:17.800
Not to be boastful, but here at the Nadesico Cafeteria,

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.980
we have over three hundred different spices and seasonings.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.660
What do you think? Isn't that something?

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.950
They even stock a nice variety of high class tea selections.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.500
It would taste even better if you add just a little bit of liquor.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.680
Admiral...

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:31.570
Oh no, you don't!

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:36.480
Well, so far the most popular dish would be

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.300
the Mars Bowl, hayashi rice with octo-alien shaped mini wieners.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:42.050
Personally, I like the chicken fried rice.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.360
Moving on, next is the hangar that houses the Aestivalis,

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:49.360
the humanoid shaped robotic weapons that the Nadesico boasts.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.640
Look at all the Aestivalis that are lined up!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.020
Hey, if you're going to talk about our cute Aesti-chan, just leave it to me!

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:58.320
First we'll start with the land combat frame!

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.730
See its amazing punches!

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.070
Behold, its awesome mobility!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.530
Oh man, so cool! A true land combat platform!

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:09.850
It even has excellent jumping abilities!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.910
Next, we have the air combat frame. And this one is even...

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.740
Hold on, right there!

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.660
Leave this baby to me, Gai-sama!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.520
This is the robot for a real hero to fight in!

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.110
Get a load of its body proportions!

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.480
The part of this baby that flies is what makes it so rad!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:25.670
Yamada-san, aren't you supposed to be...

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.790
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.060
And its killer move... All together now!

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:30.510
GAI

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.550
SUPER

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:36.210
NAPALM!

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.110
I haven't had this much fun in a while!

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.950
This Aestivalis has a special secret.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:49.860
And that's...

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.780
Cross Crash!

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.640
World peace is now at hand!

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:04.670
What the hell does that mean?

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.730
I've ridden on an artillery frame with Akito-san!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.930
I just love how this baby's so massive and heavy!

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.850
A total of four Zero-G frames were assigned to us.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.290
Our main pilots are Tenkawa Akito, Subaru Ryoko, Amano Hikaru,

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.350
and Maki lzumi, totaling four.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:33.240
Gotcha!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:40.780
I don't believe it! Only three out of ten?!

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.110
Looks like Batta-kun's fields have been reinforced as well.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:45.250
Weapons that evolve?

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:49.130
No problem!

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:50.710
We're one up on them when it comes to hand-to-hand combat!

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:53.760
What about Tenkawa? Tenkawa?!

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.580
Tenkawa!

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.900
The Aestivalis that came to my rescue was the very newest type.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.090
What the hell type of frame is this!?

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.940
A new model already?

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.400
The head's different!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.860
The generator is more compact!

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.080
And, oh, she's so smooth.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.330
Keep it up, loser!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.670
At the same time, Akatsuki Nagare joined us as the new pilot.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.790
And also Erina Kinjo Won.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.940
You know that these two must be up to something.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.380
Their true nature, their goals,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.680
everything about the army of unmanned weapons is shrouded in mystery.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:40.270
Mankind named the first alien civilization it encountered,

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.680
the Jovian Lizards.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.000
It's heading at you!

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:25.600
What?!

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:41.990
With the right angle of incidence...

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.160
Gekigan Shoot!

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.770
So somehow we've managed to get by.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:11:00.460
But will we be able to deal with Jovian weapons that continue to evolve?

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:03.520
Oh, don't you just love anime? It's so imaginative!

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.560
Wow, the fighting sequences are pretty realistic.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.900
I wonder what's going to happen to them next?!

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.750
What's wrong, Prince Akara!?

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.170
When will you have the Earth conquered?!

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:33.480
Yes, Sire. I am currently in the process of preparing a plan

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.670
through collecting cultural information about the Earthlings.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.170
Information about the Earthlings? Sounds interesting.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.040
I will be waiting for good news.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:45.190
Well, why don't we leave it at that regarding cold data?

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:49.150
With 214 living and sleeping together in the Nadesico,

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.800
various interesting things happen.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:54.500
Quite interesting things.

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:57.830
It looks like the relationship between the Captain and Tenkawa-kun

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.740
has some interesting background to it.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:02.440
Me?!

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.790
I'm sorry! I'm terribly sorry!

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.710
I'm really sorry about this. How can you ever forgive me?!

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.130
Did you hurt anything?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.720
It looks like Tenkawa-kun and Captain

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.280
were childhood friends.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.840
Have we met before?

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.180
Yes, we have!

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.130
Akito!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.650
What's wrong? Does your tummy hurt?

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:34.920
Shut up!

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:35.950
Were you in a fight?

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:37.690
Shut up! Go away!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.240
Hey...

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.450
Want to learn a magic trick that'll turn Akito back to normal?

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:50.890
Close your eyes.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.370
Baka! What did you do that for?!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:03.720
Goody, Akito's back to normal!
Baka! What did you do that for?!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.190
Goody, Akito's back to normal!

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:07.550
You...

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.860
Hey, wait a...

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:18.580
Damn!

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:34.310
Damn, I had no idea all this was going on!

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:37.840
I always take her place when she's busy! And all for what?!

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:39.960
Yes, yes. Keep cool now.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.230
How I envy those youths.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.760
And you know, while they might fight all the time,

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.600
they sure seem to connect pretty well.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.350
What was the point of us coming to Mars?

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.740
Akito, I'm sorry. I'm so sorry!

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.940
I couldn't save them at all!

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:08.170
Yurika...

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:15.170
This is the first time

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.900
that you've been nice to me since we came aboard the Nadesico.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.710
Stop it! Pull yourself together!

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:21.890
Akito...

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.140
Could you give me a kiss?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.680
Yurika? What are you saying?

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.810
If you could give me a kiss, that'd keep me going.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.440
It would keep me going just a little longer.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.470
Akito-san!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.120
Akito-san's in love with me, right?!

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:44.860
What about me?

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.540
It's me!

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:48.230
No, me!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:54.350
I guess it's rough being an adult with all those relationships.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:56.460
There you are.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.920
Thank you, Ruri-Ruri.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:14:59.960
Again?

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.850
There are nice things about being an adult too.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.230
That's right.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.040
Hey, I just remembered. You looked wonderful with those rabbit ears.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.470
You were watching?

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:14.880
I must say, a lot certainly happens here.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:15.890
A lot of nice things.

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:19.310
Nice adult things!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.280
Nice things...

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.190
It's on me.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.530
Tenkawa!

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:30.420
Tenkawa?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.240
Shut up, you two! I've had enough of this!

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:33.530
Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa!
Shut up, you two! I've had enough of this!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.970
Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa! Tenkawa!

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.460
Oh dear, what stress.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:16:02.020
Akito!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.200
Full of so much love and passion, the battleship Nadesico sails on.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.380
Where will she go?

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.860
What will be the fate of the love between those two?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.250
Someday, I'll be like that with Akara-sama.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:20.230
But Akara-sama never even notices the love I have for him.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:25.080
Mie, have you been able to collect data on Earthling culture?

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.530
Yes, Sire!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:29.390
I believe this anime, "Martian Successor Nadesico,"

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:33.430
to be the best source regarding the nature of Earthlings.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.050
Anime? What is this anime?

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:39.100
It's a form of Earth entertainment that uses pictures to tell a story.

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:43.160
They're such fools to be infatuated with whimsical fantasy.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.060
What the hell are you doing, Tenkawa?!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.160
I'm sorry!

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:49.860
I see Earthlings are made up of men and women as well.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.300
Delicate love romances that spring up amid war...

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:53.950
It's so romantic!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:54.990
Foolishness!

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.080
All this love, this romance...

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.750
How can you win battles when occupied by such folly, low life Earth scum?

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.160
Akara-sama...

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.210
What's this?!

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.950
What was that, Mie-Mie?

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.270
Sire! According to our data,

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:13.020
it appears to be an enemy formation penetration technique

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:16.090
that uses the distortion field, a form of force field.

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:18.290
I see.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.490
Penetration by using the force of a repelling energy...

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.780
I like it.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:27.330
To think that a plan that will rid us of Gekiganger could have come from this.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:29.270
You have served me well, Mie-Mie!

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:33.320
Please, Sire. Such gracious words...

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:33.730
Big Akara Special

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:37.680
Ready His Highness Akara's custom mech, the Big Akara Special, for launch!

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:42.070
Just wait, my dear Gekiganger!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.610
Professor, a UFO is closing in on the laboratory at a ferociously fast pace!

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.460
What?! Raise the barrier!

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:58.300
That won't do you any good!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.220
Distortion field!

00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:05.390
What's that?

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:06.480
Is it an earthquake?!

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:07.940
Ken, Joe, Akira!

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:10.920
We're under attack by a mecha monster! Launch and intercept immediately!

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:12.070
Roger!

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.680
What's wrong, Gekiganger?

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.760
I'll finish this off unless you come out.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.110
It's checkmate!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:20.690
Hold on!

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:22.080
Let's Gekiga-in!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.270
Gekigan Beam!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.920
No manner of attack such as that will have any effect on me!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:35.470
Take this!

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.390
Damn!

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.430
Gekigan Sword!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:43.340
Passion Slash!

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:55.950
Surely no toy such as that will be able to compromise this distortion field.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.860
Die, Gekiganger!

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:01.630
Father, they'll be defeated at this rate!

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.370
I'll finish you off!!

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.160
What should I do?

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:07.540
Ken!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:08.290
Professor!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.460
This was completed only recently, and it hasn't even been tested,

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.840
but we have no choice!

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:14.920
Ken, Joe, Akira!

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.010
Do the Gekigan Flare!

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:18.430
Gekigan Flare?

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.530
That's right.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:23.810
I anticipated something like this, so I secretly developed the Gekigan Flare!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.290
But be careful!

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:28.220
The three of you must be perfectly synchronized,

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.360
or the Gekiganger will explode!

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.810
But I guess we'll have to go for it!

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:37.670
Watch out!

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.660
Right! Here we go!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:40.900
Roger!

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:43.160
Gekigan Flare!

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.880
What is this light?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:57.030
Akara-sama, you must escape! Akara-sama!

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:04.850
Damn you, Earthlings! Just you remember this!

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.130
We did it, everyone!

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:15.150
But Professor, how did you come up with an attack like that?

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:17.790
They had it on Nadesico just recently.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.350
What? You watch it too, Professor?!

00:20:20.350 --> 00:20:21.870
Well...

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.530
In any case, come right home!

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:26.190
Your Toshikoshi Soba is all ready!

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:27.700
Yes! Soba!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.540
Do you have Moji ready too?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:29.570
The End

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:30.750
That's for tomorrow!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:35.400
The End

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.670
Is an ending like this proper?

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:38.130
The End

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.710
Why not?

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.440
So please watch us again next time.

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:50.210
Hello, I'm Kuwashima Houko, and I play Misumaru Yurika.

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:52.270
It's been rather chilly these days,

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.350
but I hope that those of you watching "Martian Successor Nadesico"

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:57.270
will blow away any encroaching colds with the gravity blast cannon!

00:21:57.270 --> 00:22:01.130
Well, next week we finally find out who the Jovian Lizards are.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:05.590
I sure hope that there'll be parts for Yurika as well.

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:07.820
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:09.470
"The Significant Other From A Star Far Away"

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:11.910
Let's watch it, everyone! Promise me, okay?
